---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Backup Status"
  description="Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recent backup status, completion times, backup types, availability and backup history."
>
  <main>
    <section class="resource-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
        <h1>Backup <span class="hero-accent">Status</span></h1>
        <p>
          Practical Oracle SQL for reviewing recent backup status, completion
          times, backup types, availability and backup history.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="resource-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="resource-intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Check whether recent backups completed as expected</h2>
          <p>
            Backup status provides the first operational view of recovery
            readiness. Start with recent RMAN jobs, then review the backup sets,
            pieces and files that were produced and their current availability.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-grid">
          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">01 &middot; JOB STATUS</div>
              <h2>Review recent backup status</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Find recent RMAN jobs and identify completed, warning or failed operations.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    session_key,
    input_type,
    status,
    start_time,
    end_time,
    time_taken_display
FROM v$rman_backup_job_details
ORDER BY start_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">02 &middot; BACKUP TYPES</div>
              <h2>Review backup activity by type</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Summarize recent RMAN activity by backup type and completion status.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    input_type,
    status,
    COUNT(*) AS job_count,
    MIN(start_time) AS first_start,
    MAX(end_time) AS last_end
FROM v$rman_backup_job_details
GROUP BY
    input_type,
    status
ORDER BY
    input_type,
    status;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">03 &middot; BACKUP SETS</div>
              <h2>Review recent backup sets</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Inspect completed backup sets, their type, level, piece count and duration.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    set_stamp,
    set_count,
    backup_type,
    incremental_level,
    pieces,
    start_time,
    completion_time,
    elapsed_seconds
FROM v$backup_set
ORDER BY completion_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">04 &middot; PIECE STATUS</div>
              <h2>Check backup piece availability</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Review the status and storage location of recently created backup pieces.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    set_stamp,
    set_count,
    piece#,
    device_type,
    handle,
    status,
    bytes,
    completion_time
FROM v$backup_piece
ORDER BY completion_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">05 &middot; BACKUP FILES</div>
              <h2>Review backup file status</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Inspect RMAN backup files and identify available, expired or unavailable entries.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    backup_type,
    file_type,
    status,
    device_type,
    completion_time,
    bytes,
    fname
FROM v$backup_files
ORDER BY completion_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 30 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>

          <article class="resource-block">
            <div class="resource-block__header">
              <div class="resource-block__label">06 &middot; BACKUP HISTORY</div>
              <h2>Review recent backup volume</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="resource-block__description">
              Compare recent backup jobs by input and output size to spot changes in backup volume.
            </p>
            <pre><code>SELECT
    input_type,
    start_time,
    end_time,
    input_bytes_display,
    output_bytes_display,
    compression_ratio
FROM v$rman_backup_job_details
WHERE status LIKE 'COMPLETED%'
ORDER BY start_time DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-note">
          <p class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; BACKUP &amp; RECOVERY</p>
          <h2>Backup status is more than a successful job message.</h2>
          <p>
            Confirm that recent jobs completed successfully, then check the
            backup sets and pieces created by those jobs. Availability and
            storage metadata provide another layer of evidence when validating
            whether backups can still be used for recovery.
          </p>
          <p>
            Oracle documents <code>V$RMAN_BACKUP_JOB_DETAILS</code> as a view
            containing details about backup jobs, while
            <code>V$BACKUP_SET</code> contains information about completed
            backup sets from the control file.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="resource-actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/backup-recovery/">
            Back to Backup &amp; Recovery
          </a>
          <a
            class="resource-actions__link"
            href="/tools/backup-recovery/archived-redo/"
          >
            Read Archived Redo
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {
    const button = document.createElement("button");
    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";
    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const code = pre.querySelector("code");
      if (!code) return;

      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");
        button.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      } catch {
        button.textContent = "Copy failed";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);
      }
    });

    pre.appendChild(button);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .resource-hero {
    padding-top: 82px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .resource-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .resource-hero .hero-accent {
    color: var(--orange);
  }

  .resource-hero > .container > p:last-child {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }

  .resource-intro {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .resource-intro .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-intro h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .resource-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    min-width: 0;
    height: 560px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    transition:
      border-color 0.22s ease,
      box-shadow 0.22s ease,
      transform 0.22s ease;
  }

  .resource-block:hover {
    border-color: #d8dce1;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(17, 29, 44, 0.06);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
  }

  .resource-block__header {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .resource-block__label {
    margin-bottom: 9px;
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .resource-block h2 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .resource-block__description {
    min-height: 48px;
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block pre {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-height: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 22px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-y: auto;
    white-space: pre;
    background: #2f353d;
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: #f3f4f6;
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .resource-block code {
    font-family: inherit;
    white-space: pre;
  }

  .resource-copy-button {
    position: absolute;
    top: 10px;
    right: 10px;
    padding: 5px 9px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #374151;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .resource-copy-button:hover {
    background: #f3f4f6;
  }

  .resource-note {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-top: 32px;
    padding: 30px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    background: #f7f8fa;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .resource-note .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note h2 {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 38px);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .resource-note p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .resource-note p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .resource-note code {
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: #eef0f2;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family:
      "Cascadia Code",
      "Consolas",
      "Courier New",
      monospace;
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }

  .resource-actions {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    margin-top: 24px;
  }

  .resource-actions__link {
    color: var(--orange);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .resource-actions__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .resource-hero {
      padding-top: 58px;
      padding-bottom: 54px;
    }

    .resource-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(38px, 12vw, 54px);
    }

    .resource-section {
      padding-top: 44px;
      padding-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block {
      height: 520px;
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-block__description {
      min-height: 0;
    }

    .resource-block pre {
      padding: 18px;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    .resource-note {
      padding: 22px;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }

    .resource-actions {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
